 "summary": "Assignments are made by lot (Service Manual 2026-2028, p. 45), but the lot follows firm rules. It skips the committees the area held in its last three terms, refills each committee to its standard size (8 or 9 members), and takes at most one new member per region on a committee. Since the December 2020 draw (Panel 71) it also spreads every committee across as many regions as possible counting both panels, and keeps neighbouring areas apart, matching GSO's 2025 criteria ('wider regional representation across all committees'; 'limit adjacent areas from different regions'). Areas from the same state or province never shared a committee in 2017-2026 (10 pairs expected without that rule). The IC/RF seat rotates within each region (one per region, alternating regions by panel), and Archives takes four members from four different regions, mildly avoiding neighbours. Honest forward-chained test on Panels 71-76 (rule strengths chosen on earlier panels only): the committee actually drawn got 22.6% on average (1 in 11 = 9.1%), was the top pick 32.1% of the time and in the top three 68.8%. GSO's \"best of five rounds\" procedure, tested as a model, did not do better than these rules.",
